      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022paragraphs\u0022:[[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The first risk is that supply constraints cap how fast strong demand turns into revenue, because management said supply chain will remain the governor of near-term revenue and that conversion is likely to be nonlinear.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by fourth-quarter revenue landing below the guided range of $1.93 billion to $1.95 billion while management continues to describe demand as not the limiter.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The second risk is that profitability normalises, because the chief financial officer cautioned that one-time tariff impacts artificially pulled up fiscal 2026 profitability and will not repeat.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by a fourth-quarter net margin below the 21.5% of the latest quarter even though revenue lands inside the guided range, or by non-GAAP earnings per share falling short of the guided $3.34 to $3.40.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The third risk is that the order momentum behind the growth does not hold, because analysts pressed on whether the elevated order level is sustainable and management\u0027s base case is only orders slightly up from the third quarter.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by fourth-quarter orders coming in below the third-quarter level, against management\u0027s base case of a slight increase.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The fourth risk is dependence on AI-driven demand in the Communications Solutions Group, which produced $1,345 million of the $1,846 million of quarterly revenue and drove the growth in commercial communications.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by Communications Solutions Group revenue falling below its latest quarterly level of $1,345 million in the fourth quarter, at a time when company guidance calls for total revenue to rise.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}]]}"
